    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "578e1c25_75d3f822",
        "filename": "src/core/SkCanvas.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 7
      },
      "lineNbr": 2316,
      "author": {
        "id": 8341
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-04-09T18:25:41Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "If this fails, but there was an image filter on the paint passed into `auto layer \u003d this-\u003eaboutToDraw` we\u0027ve created a device and layer that will be restored when `layer` goes out of scope. It won\u0027t have had anything drawn into it, but will still then run through the image filtering with a transparent black image, which probably will produce transparent black (unless the specific filters change that).\n\nWe can\u0027t just return `AutoLayerForImageFilter(in_place, this, layer-\u003epaint(), \u0026bounds, /*skip\u003d*/false)` here to add a deeper layer, since then the first layer still gets destroyed too soon. What we will need to add is a way to modify the AutoLayerForImageFilter object to redo its mask filter layering. That should be as simple as making `addMaskFilterLayer()` public so we can add it to the auto-layer if the analytic blur fails, and then return `layer` that now includes both image filter and mask filter layers.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 2316,
        "startChar": 7,
        "endLine": 2316,
        "endChar": 9
      },
      "revId": "3267b25ef32fc627aa431d8cc0d36b8e6e1d209d",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
